---
import LegalLayout from "../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { getTranslations } from "../../i18n";

const lang = "en";
const t = getTranslations(lang);
---

<LegalLayout
  title={t.meta.privacyTitle}
  description="SliceBill Privacy Policy — how we collect, use, and protect your personal data."
  lang={lang}
  lastUpdated="November 20, 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
  <p>
    The controller of your personal data is <strong>DARDAN SP. Z O.O.</strong>, a company registered in Poland, with its registered office at ul. Lewandowskiej 68, 43-143 Lędziny, Poland (NIP: 6462933321, KRS: 0000497120).
  </p>
  <p>
    Contact: <a href="mailto:support@slicebill.app">support@slicebill.app</a>
  </p>

  <h2>2. What Data We Collect</h2>
  <h3>Data you provide voluntarily</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Email address</strong> — when you create an account with email/password or sign in with Google or Sign in with Apple</li>
    <li><strong>Display name / nickname</strong> — chosen by you in app settings</li>
    <li><strong>Profile avatar</strong> — optional SVG avatar generated locally on your device from a chosen seed — the app does not upload profile photos or call external avatar APIs</li>
    <li><strong>Expense and group data</strong> — group names, expenses, amounts, currencies, payments, and member names you enter</li>
    <li><strong>Receipt photos (AI Receipt Scanner)</strong> — voluntarily submitted JPEG, PNG, or WebP images (iOS HEIC images are converted on-device), processed by Google Cloud Vertex AI (Gemini) in <code>europe-central2</code> (Warsaw) to extract line items and totals. Images are not permanently stored on our servers by default; any optional diagnostic samples stored under an active technical flag are deleted upon account deletion</li>
    <li><strong>Feedback & bug reports</strong> — messages and optional contact email submitted voluntarily via the in-app feedback form</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Data collected automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Firebase Authentication & Firestore logs</strong> — sign-in events, IP address, device type, and operation timestamps (server-side only, for security and service delivery)</li>
    <li><strong>Firebase Crashlytics (mobile apps)</strong> — crash logs, stack traces, and non-fatal authentication error telemetry used to improve app stability</li>
    <li><strong>Push notification tokens (FCM)</strong> — stored only when you opt in to notifications in app settings</li>
    <li><strong>Firebase App Check & abuse prevention</strong> — device/browser attestation tokens (Google Play Integrity, Apple App Attest/DeviceCheck, Google reCAPTCHA Enterprise) and temporary daily IP rate-limit records for unauthenticated mobile guest scans (automatically purged daily at midnight)</li>
    <li><strong>Local & offline storage</strong> — local-only groups, language/theme/currency preferences, and pending offline writes stored on your device (Hive CE and Firestore offline cache)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not use advertising trackers, third-party marketing analytics platforms (such as Google Analytics or Meta Pixel), or sell your data to any third party.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>3. Why We Process Your Data (Legal Basis)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contract performance (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR)</strong> — to provide the SliceBill service, including account management, expense syncing (including offline edits), AI receipt scanning, and group collaboration.</li>
    <li><strong>Consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR)</strong> — for optional features such as push notifications or optional product communications. You may withdraw consent at any time in app settings or via the email unsubscribe link.</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR)</strong> — for protecting the service against bots and abuse (App Check, scan rate limits), diagnosing crashes (Crashlytics), and infrastructure security.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. How Long We Keep Your Data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Account and cloud group data is retained as long as your account is active.</li>
    <li>After account deletion, your personal data is promptly deleted or anonymized as described in Section 5, except where longer retention is required by tax or accounting law.</li>
    <li>Temporary anti-abuse rate-limit records for unauthenticated mobile scans (<code>ip_rate_limits</code>) are automatically deleted daily at midnight Warsaw time.</li>
    <li>Local-only mode data (groups created without an account) is stored exclusively on your device and is not transmitted to our servers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Account and Personal Data Deletion</h2>
  <p>
    SliceBill users have the right to request permanent deletion of their account and associated personal data at any time.
  </p>
  <h3>How to request account deletion?</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>In the app:</strong> Go to <strong>Settings -&gt; Delete Account</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> Send an email from the address associated with your account to <a href="mailto:support@slicebill.app">support@slicebill.app</a> with the subject "Account deletion request".</li>
  </ol>
  <h3>What data will be deleted?</h3>
  <p>
    Upon confirmation, we irreversibly delete: your user profile, email address, nickname reservation, private cloud offline groups, FCM device tokens, invite links you created, receipt scan quota/samples, and we unsubscribe your email from Brevo.
  </p>
  <p>
    In shared public groups with other active members, your personal identity links (<code>uid</code>, email, avatar seed) are severed and the historical participant is marked <strong>"(deleted)"</strong> so remaining members do not lose settlement history (if no other registered members remain, the group is deleted completely). Voluntary tip billing records required by tax law (e.g. Stripe or mobile store records) are retained as required by applicable regulations.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Data Sharing</h2>
  <p>To operate SliceBill, we share necessary data only with the following trusted processors:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Firebase & Google Cloud</strong> (Google LLC) — authentication (Auth), database (Firestore), Cloud Functions and Hosting in <code>europe-central2</code> (Warsaw), push notifications (FCM), crash diagnostics (Crashlytics), App Check security (Play Integrity, reCAPTCHA Enterprise), and <strong>Vertex AI (Gemini)</strong> in <code>europe-central2</code> for AI receipt parsing.</li>
    <li><strong>Brevo (Sendinblue SAS, France / EU)</strong> — transactional emails (account verification, password reset, group invitations, supporter thank-you emails) and optional product updates (unsubscribe anytime; auto-unsubscribed upon account deletion).</li>
    <li><strong>Stripe</strong> (Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd. / Stripe, Inc.) — processing voluntary web tips ("Buy Me a Coffee"); SliceBill never stores payment card numbers.</li>
    <li><strong>RevenueCat, Inc. & Apple App Store / Google Play</strong> — processing and verifying voluntary mobile in-app tips ("Buy Me a Coffee") on iOS and Android.</li>
    <li><strong>Frankfurter API (ECB rates)</strong> — public exchange rate lookup (only currency codes are transmitted, with no personal user data).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We never sell or share your data with data brokers or advertising networks.</p>

  <h2>7. Your Rights Under GDPR</h2>
  <p>You have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> your personal data</li>
    <li><strong>Rectify</strong> inaccurate data</li>
    <li><strong>Erase</strong> your data ("right to be forgotten")</li>
    <li><strong>Restrict</strong> processing</li>
    <li><strong>Data portability</strong> — receive your data in a machine-readable format (e.g. PDF/CSV group expense exports)</li>
    <li><strong>Object</strong> to processing based on legitimate interests</li>
    <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time (for consent-based processing)</li>
    <li><strong>Lodge a complaint</strong> with the Polish supervisory authority (UODO): <a href="https://uodo.gov.pl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">uodo.gov.pl</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>To exercise your rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:support@slicebill.app">support@slicebill.app</a>.</p>

  <h2>8. Data Security</h2>
  <p>
    We apply multi-layered technical safeguards, including encrypted transport (HTTPS/TLS), <strong>Firebase App Check</strong> attestation (Apple App Attest, Google Play Integrity, reCAPTCHA Enterprise), strict Firebase Security Rules allowlists limiting read/write access to authorized owners, atomic server-side transactions, and expiring 256-bit group invite tokens.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>
    SliceBill is not intended for users under 13 years of age. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of material changes by updating the "Last updated" date above. Continued use of SliceBill after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    DARDAN SP. Z O.O.<br />
    ul. Lewandowskiej 68, 43-143 Lędziny, Poland<br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:support@slicebill.app">support@slicebill.app</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
